  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760279,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "### IGDB - 1984-F (Commodore 64)\n\n**Embark on a perilous quest in this classic text adventure!** *IGDB*, a faithful computer adaptation of Ian Livingstone’s *Fighting Fantasy* gamebook #3, plunges you into a world of danger and intrigue on the Commodore 64. As a wary adventurer, you’re drawn into a desperate mission: retrieve the lost Dwarfish Runes of the Ancients from the treacherous Darkwood Forest.\n\nFollowing a fateful encounter with a dying dwarf, you seek aid from the wise wizard Yaztromo, who equips you with essential magical gear. Your journey is fraught with peril, as you must navigate a sprawling, scroll-driven narrative filled with branching paths and challenging choices. \n\nForget dice rolls! *IGDB* automates the traditional *Fighting Fantasy* mechanics, managing your character’s statistics, inventory, and combat prowess.  Start with a sword and nine meals, then face hordes of hill trolls and uncover ancient secrets.  Will you succeed in saving Stonebridge and its people, or become another victim of the Darkwood’s shadows?  Prepare for a thrilling, interactive adventure!"
    },
